    "version_first_page_text": "                                  LIS3DH\n\n                   MEMS digital output motion sensor:\n    ultra-low-power high-performance 3-axis \"nano\" accelerometer\n                                                                       Datasheet - production data\n\n                                                      Display orientation\n                                                      Gaming and virtual reality input devices\n                                                      Impact recognition and logging\n                                                      Vibration monitoring and compensation\n\n          /*$     [ [ PP            Description\n\n                                          The LIS3DH is an ultra-low-power high-\nFeatures                                    performance three-axis linear accelerometer                                                  belonging to the “nano” family, with digital I2C/SPI\n  Wide supply voltage, 1.71 V to 3.6 V                serial interface standard output. The device\n                                                     features ultra-low-power operational modes that  Independent IO supply (1.8 V) and supply\n                                                     allow advanced power saving and smart   voltage compatible\n                                         embedded functions.\n  Ultra-low-power mode consumption\n                                          The LIS3DH has dynamically user-selectable full  down to 2 μA\n                                                   scales of 2g/±4g/8g/16g and is capable of\n  2g/±4g/8g/16g dynamically selectable full                                               measuring accelerations with output data rates\n   scale                                                from 1 Hz to 5.3 kHz. The self-test capability\n  I2C/SPI digital output interface                    allows the user to check the functioning of the\n  16-bit data output                              sensor in the final application. The device may be\n                                                    configured to generate interrupt signals using two\n  2 independent programmable interrupt                                                independent inertial wake-up/free-fall events as\n   generators for free-fall and motion detection                                                        well as by the position of the device itself.\n  6D/4D orientation detection                     Thresholds and timing of interrupt generators are\n  Free-fall detection                           programmable by the end user on the fly. The\n                                         LIS3DH has an integrated 32-level first-in, first-\n  Motion detection                                                    out (FIFO) buffer allowing the user to store data in\n  Embedded temperature sensor                   order to limit intervention by the host processor.\n  Embedded self-test                        The LIS3DH is available in small thin plastic land\n                                                          grid array package (LGA) and is guaranteed to\n  Embedded 32 levels of 16-bit data output FIFO                                                  operate over an extended temperature range\n  10000 g high shock survivability                 from -40 °C to +85 °C.\n ECOPACK®, RoHS and “Green” compliant\n                                                          Table 1. Device summary\nApplications                                 Order codes    Temp.    Package  Packaging\n                                                               range [C]\n  Motion activated functions\n                                              LIS3DHTR    -40 to +85   LGA-16  Tape and reel\n  Free-fall detection\n  Click/double-click recognition\n  Intelligent power saving for handheld devices\n  Pedometers\n\n\nDecember 2016                          DocID17530 Rev 2                                        1/54\n\nThis is information on a product in full production.                                                                         www.st.com"
  },
